## 2. Setup

One week of continuous use on real work — shipping a Python SDK, a Cloudflare Worker, a
Next.js site — not a benchmark. That is the study's strength and its main weakness, and both
are addressed in §7.

- **Readings:** {readings_all} total; {readings} in the analyzable era.
- **Runs:** {runs}.
- **Calibration:** `goal_min = 0.30` (overlap floor), `stall_window = 4`, `settled_max = 0.15`.
  Published and unchanged for the study period; a threshold moved mid-corpus makes every
  reading before and after incomparable.

**Two logging eras, never pooled.** Until 2026-07-28 only drift moments were written, so
every row was a fire and `drifting` did not exist as a field. Afterwards every step is
logged. {pre_era} readings predate the change and are excluded from every rate below. We
report this prominently because pooling them produced three wrong statistics in one sitting,
including a fire rate quoted as 22% that is really {fire_rate}%.

