## Availability

`laserbrain` on PyPI. Corpus tooling — `corpus-map.py`, `label-fires.py`, `sensitivity.py`,
`replay.py` — ships alongside. The drift log is local and unshared; the labelling rules are
runnable against any corpus of the same shape.

## Related work

Goal drift as a measured failure mode: Arike et al., *Evaluating Goal Drift in Language Model
Agents* (AIES). Asymmetric drift under value conflict (ICLR 2026 workshop). Architectural
re-anchoring and goal persistence: Zylos, *Goal Persistence and Goal Drift in Long-Horizon AI
Agents* (2026). Deterministic enforcement at the tool boundary: the agentic-guardrails
literature, incl. AgentSpec and Pro2Guard. Closest in structure: *AgentTether* (arXiv
2607.06273), whose Check mechanism covers loop repetition, intent drift and expectation
deviation against an intent fixed at initialization — reached with embeddings, an LLM
evaluator and a constructed execution graph, where this work uses set overlap and no model
call.
